          "line": "solid",
          "arrow": "end"
        },
        {
          "kind": "edge",
          "from": "d",
          "to": "f",
          "via": "straight",
          "line": "solid",
          "arrow": "end"
        },
        {
          "kind": "edge",
          "from": "d",
          "to": "e",
          "via": "curve",
          "line": "dashed",
          "arrow": "none",
          "label": "doubts remain"
        },
        {
          "kind": "edge",
          "from": "e",
          "to": "f",
          "via": "curve",
          "line": "dashed",
          "arrow": "end",
          "label": "yet it worked"
        }
      ],
      "caption": "A ladder of ever-subtler linguistic mastery climbing toward human-level loss, with an unresolved doubt hanging off it and an open question at the top."
    },
    {
      "id": "inside-agency",
      "title": "Agency From Data",
      "height": 920,
      "items": [
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "a",
          "shape": "ellipse",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "GPT-3 learns to roleplay agents",
          "size": "sm",
          "detail": "Trained on human-generated text, it inevitably learns to imitate goal-pursuing agents when prompted.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-hfcz8w"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "b",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 100,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "Agency is built from atoms",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "no principled boundary",
          "detail": "Since agents are made of non-agentic matter, no data can be guaranteed free of agency.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-yb6wsc"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 180,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "We model rivers as agents too",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "the intentional stance",
          "detail": "Humans routinely use teleological, agent-like explanations for non-agentic natural systems.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-frehf0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "d",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "Systems 'want' to optimize",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "variational shortcuts",
          "detail": "Treating a system as maximizing some quantity is a computationally cheap, powerful shortcut a network could learn.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-tyue6z"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "e",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 340,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "But such shortcuts cost compute",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "only pay off at scale",
          "detail": "Variational reasoning only emerges when a problem is rich and repeated enough to beat memorization.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-wkqdua"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "f",
          "shape": "diamond",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 420,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 70,
          "text": "What data induces agency?",
          "size": "sm",
          "detail": "An open empirical question: how much diversity pushes a model from safe modeling into agency.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-ufadea"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "g",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 520,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "Game of Life invites 'gliders'",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "cellular automata",
          "detail": "Even a simple rule-based system naturally decomposes into agent-like entities pursuing trajectories.",
          "tone": 3,
          "block": "spya-myjtg3"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "tm",
          "shape": "diamond",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 600,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "What about Turing machines?",
          "size": "sm",
          "detail": "Pushed to the most general computational setting: does training on program traces risk agency?",
          "tone": 3,
          "block": "spya-q88ypt"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "h",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 700,
          "w": 220,
          "h": 70,
          "text": "One machine: just follows rules",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "no clear agency",
          "detail": "A single random Turing machine simply runs; nothing in it is trying to maximize or minimize anything.",
          "tone": 2,
          "block": "spya-etcjwv"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "i",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 480,
          "y": 700,
          "w": 220,
          "h": 70,
          "text": "Many machines: infer intent",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "a rudimentary theory of mind",
          "detail": "Meta-learning over many programs forces the model to infer each one's underlying 'intent' from behavior.",
          "tone": 3,
          "block": "spya-yzb32b"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "j",
          "shape": "ellipse",
          "x": 260,
          "y": 810,
          "w": 240,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Agency is hard to exclude",
          "size": "md",
          "sub": "like Turing-completeness itself",
          "detail": "Agency is a convergent, useful capability; the broader and more powerful the system, the harder it is to keep out.",
          "tone": 3,
          "block": "spya-c8qwnc"
        },
